    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Fisher College is a private college situated in Boston, Massachusetts. Fisher College welcomes international students from all over the world to the university. Founded in 1903, Fisher College is one of the leading bachelor's and master's degree-granting institutions in Boston.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>On-campus accommodation is offered at three different buildings: 116 Beacon Street, 118 Beacon Street, and 70 Charlesgate East. The residence halls contain fully furnished rooms with a choice of single or double beds and all other standard student amenities. Communal lounge, kitchen and bathroom areas are also located in these residences, with resident assistants on hand to help with all enquiries.</p><p>Fisher College also has partnerships with several rental apartments and houses in the wider area. Students can contact the college for administrative help and advice for finding suitable off-campus accommodation within their budget.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sports",
      "value": "<p>The fitness center and gymnasium are two other fitness spaces where students can benefit from healthy exercise. The Fisher cafe is the main food outlet on campus, but there are other dietary preferences for students to choose from.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lab",
      "value": "<p>The Department of Information Services provides the college with computer laboratories, technical training, network support, and more so students can make the most of technological innovation. Science laboratories are also located on campus for students to utilize.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Library",
      "value": "<p>A media center and a writing center are two buildings of note, and the Fisher College library has a range of books, films and other resources within an aesthetic environment.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student Life",
      "value": "<p>Campus life provides many opportunities for students to socialize together and lead a well-balanced life. From yoga club to becoming a part of the student center and beyond, students can pursue their interests and make friends alongside their studies.</p><p>Volunteering opportunities around campus help all students to feel a part of the community as they lead the change in making a difference. Students often meet over breakfast or dinner in the Dining Hall, with a range of hot food, deli sandwiches and more treats on offer to students and staff.</p>",
